    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, I added a duplicate-email check that rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, returning **409 Conflict**.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **New helper `isEmailAlreadyUsed`** (near the existing `normalizeEmail`): returns `true` when the given email is non-null and matches any existing owner's email, comparing case-insensitively on the lower-cased value.\n\n2. **The check itself** in `addOwner`, placed right after email normalization (which lower-cases the incoming email) and the telephone-conflict check, alongside the other 409 rules:\n```java\nif (isEmailAlreadyUsed(owner.getEmail())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\nOwners with no email (`null`) are unaffected, since the spec only concerns emails already in use. `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes, and the full suite builds green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
